            ],
            "evidence": [
              {
                "reference": "doi:10.1128/JB.06130-11",
                "supports": "SUPPORT",
                "explanation": "Mayer et al. 2012 explicitly cultivates the DSM 18386 type strain in 1/2 SME-Ignicoccus medium, the medium this record represents. Ingredient-level recipe is cited transitively (Paper et al. 2007), so parent-formulation identity is strong by name but not printed in this source. | Identifiers: DSM 18386T; RefSeq NC_009776.1; 16S Gene ID 5562932",
                "snippet": "I. hospitalis KIN4/IT (DSM 18386) was grown in 1/2 SME-Ignicoccus medium at 90C under H2/CO2 (80:20, v/v) at 250 kPa, H2 as electron donor and elemental sulfur as electron acceptor."
              }
            ]
          },
